From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Default the terminal font to the system's fixed-pitch one

The default terminal font family is the string "Monospace", which is a
fontconfig alias. Windows has no fontconfig, so Qt matches nothing, falls
back to a proportional face, and qtermwidget prints on every start:

    Using a variable-width font in the terminal.  This may cause performance
    degradation and display/alignment errors.

It is not only noise -- the terminal really is rendering in a variable-width
font, which is what the message is about. The default cannot be right here,
because the name it uses does not exist on this platform.

QFontDatabase::systemFont(QFontDatabase::FixedFont) is Qt asking the platform
the same question the alias asks fontconfig. Only the default changes; an
explicit choice in Options is untouched.

Guarded on Windows: "Monospace" resolves correctly where fontconfig exists,
and changing a visible default is not this patch's business there.
diff --git a/src/settingsmanager.cpp b/src/settingsmanager.cpp
index 55e661a..a1fe763 100644
--- a/src/settingsmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/settingsmanager.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include <QStringList>
 #include <QVariant>
 #include <QSettings>
+#include <QFontDatabase>
 #include <QDir>
 #include <QCryptographicHash>
 
@@ -742,7 +743,17 @@ QString SettingsManager::getTerminalColorScheme()
 
 QString SettingsManager::getTerminalFontFamily()
 {
+#ifdef Q_OS_WIN
+  // "Monospace" is a fontconfig alias. Windows has no fontconfig, so Qt
+  // substitutes a proportional face and qtermwidget says so on every start:
+  // "Using a variable-width font in the terminal." Ask Qt for the system's
+  // fixed-pitch font instead, which is what the alias means anywhere.
+  static const QString fixedFamily =
+      QFontDatabase::systemFont(QFontDatabase::FixedFont).family();
+  return (instance()->getSYSsettings()->value(ctn_KEY_TERMINAL_FONT_FAMILY, fixedFamily)).toString();
+#else
   return (instance()->getSYSsettings()->value(ctn_KEY_TERMINAL_FONT_FAMILY, QStringLiteral("Monospace"))).toString();
+#endif
 }
 
 qreal SettingsManager::getTerminalFontPointSize()
